From 4fedb68ff3a9b115d4932d47c09dca68c56fa77c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abinash Haldorai <abinash.haldorai@eka.care>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:57:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Voice: authenticate the telephony answer webhook and
 audio socket

/voice/answer was open to anyone who knew an agent id, and the Vobiz
audio WebSocket authenticated on session existence alone (the token was
accepted and ignored), so anyone who learned a session id could attach.

Add a shared secret, VOICE_TELEPHONY_SECRET in the MATRIX config:
- /answer requires ?key=<secret> (403 otherwise) and returns a WebSocket
  URL carrying a short-lived HMAC token bound to the new session id;
- the WebSocket checks that token before looking up the session and
  closes with 4001 if it is missing, wrong, expired or for another
  session.

Nothing is enforced until the secret is set, so deploying this changes
nothing by itself; a warning is logged on each call while it is unset.
Update the Vobiz answer URL before setting the secret.

Not tested against a live Vobiz account: unit tests cover the module,
the answer route and the socket gate with mocks.

